5bfe1d0b9228ff08748db87a8592f899a8ed6b78bdc252efb5"},"seconds":30.37036156654358,"seed":506428756815346764,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\( k \\) given that the remainder when \\( kx^4 + 9x^3 + kx^2 + 32x - 11 \\) is divided by \\( x + 5 \\) is 4, we can use the Remainder Theorem. The Remainder Theorem states that the remainder of the division of a polynomial \\( f(x) \\) by \\( x - c \\) is \\( f(c) \\).\n\nIn this case, we are given that the remainder when dividing by \\( x + 5 \\) (which can be written as \\( x - (-5) \\)) is 4. Therefore, we need to evaluate the polynomial at \\( x = -5 \\) and set it equal to 4.\n\nLet \\( f(x) = kx^4 + 9x^3 + kx^2 + 32x - 11 \\). According to the Remainder Theorem:\n\\[ f(-5) = 4 \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( x = -5 \\) into \\( f(x) \\):\n\\[ f(-5) = k(-5)^4 + 9(-5)^3 + k(-5)^2 + 32(-5) - 11 \\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\\[ (-5)^4 = 625 \\]\n\\[ (-5)^3 = -125 \\]\n\\[ (-5)^2 = 25 \\]\n\nSubstitute these values back into the equation:\n\\[ f(-5) = k(625) + 9(-125) + k(25) + 32(-5) - 11 \\]\n\\[ f(-5) = 625k - 1125 + 25k - 160 - 11 \\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[ f(-5) = 650k - 1296 \\]\n\nSet this equal to 4:\n\\[ 650k - 1296 = 4 \\]\n\nSolve for \\( k \\):\n\\[ 650k = 1300 \\]\n\\[ k = \\frac{1300}{650} \\]\n\\[ k = 2 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( k \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
